{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 AMC 10A #15</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">2024 AMC 12A #9</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Quadratic_Residues,_Answer_Choices_rather_than_finding_)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Quadratic Residues, Answer Choices rather than finding )</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Apex_STEM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Apex STEM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast!_About_3_min_solve!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast! About 3 min solve!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(4_min_solve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (4 min solve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the greatest integer such that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6714463de67fa9c6439d5e31867fa5048f4c20cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2499f64ed0073ce407d3ed27dce7b4a037e92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> are perfect squares. What is the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc209ca9d96cd32011748a9aa6b40d3bce51d5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf1381a94c543791fb2ee16c99964b31efded8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213=P^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d163d3af49308d06b2976a6a440d6765fa1692ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773=Q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> for some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b727b773d199f4fa0d684957a720f9c3e9750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> We subtract the first equation from the second, then apply the difference of squares: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808b886dfcc0c467f633a6e01b1d195b732cd4df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(Q+P)(Q-P)=2560.\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7ef7781259d435c0dd411f0d78a700b4de2804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q+P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd540e103248ddd9a39f7cf20540bd848bd6180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q-P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> have the same parity, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aead94e74dbf0ee281bc481d37e8692c8053f8ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q+P&gt;Q-P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>We wish to maximize both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5646f1d6eed76fee4840dacf4c8fb39ef64fe46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> so we maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7ef7781259d435c0dd411f0d78a700b4de2804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q+P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9011c0e11a679f09cce16084ba972c5bce4f57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q-P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f556e8231a340e1d4f8ff162f163396601622db3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Q+P&amp;=1280, \\\\ Q-P&amp;=2, \\end{align*}\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d05fae77fddb03c1705734c1f165c46a8a5e651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P,Q)=(639,641).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Finally, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/4074c7b1d9fd9f392e3ffd95de35df64d0456d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=P^2-1213=Q^2-3773\\equiv1-3\\equiv8\\pmod{10},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"415\" height=\"21\" /> so the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76d48d78e1726b4b56561f94556b517bfe4290d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM \n</p><p>~Tacos_are_yummy_1\n</p><p>~minor edit\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ideally, we would like for the two squares to be as close as possible. The best case is that they are consecutive squares (no square numbers in between them); however, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6714463de67fa9c6439d5e31867fa5048f4c20cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2499f64ed0073ce407d3ed27dce7b4a037e92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> (and thus their square roots) have the same parity, they cannot be consecutive squares (which are always opposite parities). The best we can do is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6714463de67fa9c6439d5e31867fa5048f4c20cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2499f64ed0073ce407d3ed27dce7b4a037e92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> have one square in between them. \n</p><p>Let the square between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6714463de67fa9c6439d5e31867fa5048f4c20cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2499f64ed0073ce407d3ed27dce7b4a037e92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. So, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de215191ee7a757bb4af2cb956de6f82e417c72e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213 = (x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84b3a1300915d0804b638afb7585626b5d782df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773 = (x+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />. Subtracting the two, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8afa2989c35341322bd85994a5f39ec350d60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(M+3773)-(M+1213) = (x+1)^2 - (x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"382\" height=\"21\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f4a5348177623206111731601987078a805aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2560 = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, which leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89afae75a9e2f6fba9eadd960ffc46490ba8886d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 640$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the two squares are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4eca5f13a8c09d0092369cb86379337b2274572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$639^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050d9c5fe3649015421dcec5ab2b26caa644d321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$641^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />, which both have units digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/decf788a80b14ca407fbf3ccfcea65e37711c3c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206ca345020c7262bf8e089709eb850296aa4b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> have units digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> will have units digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129c1c4cbf3d35dbd549e42c49762617b1b73022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~i_am_suk_at_math_2 (parity argument editing by Technodoggo)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/640c3e74caf66e903f7b1985910fe27ae70abde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213=N^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d5164d80145e8df6f5789bc87e4c086e69a17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow M+3773=(N+a)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0eb28666e3cbe3e4c173fb5b212c5ad539a3d50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> by parity\n</p><p>Thus, the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is 2\nWhich gives us,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2270b4c5eecaac125c469883e8a259bf9dc80eb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(N+a)^2-N^2=M+3773-(M+1213)\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e755afe2cfc903583d925e6b9612901fb1a6b910.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4N+4=2560\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8236f3d26551913a654f50511bba37d179700e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N=639\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />\nPlugging this back in,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c3904cbd111031276094111e3b1bac18821cc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M=N^2-1213 \\space \\mod \\space 10\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fea7eeed3647a49fdd175a64198fcd1dbc5fff0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M=8 \\space \\mod \\space 10\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"12\" />\nHence the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129c1c4cbf3d35dbd549e42c49762617b1b73022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~lptoggled\n</p><p>- trevian1(minor edit)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e44ee344040dda41e58b9162d81c8c15e2468b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1213=n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4d5b3555de84b0449f8e5d7bc6af43187bce0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773=(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We do this because, in order to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the perfect squares need to be as close to each other as possible. We find that this configuration doesn't work, as when we subtract the equations, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc926971cf36f24570a49d2f997015a7626cea3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+1=2560$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />; impossible. Then we try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e9890cc2e82c9460c3dd2aae1c2704106eac59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+3773=(n+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />. Now we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49da742dc7a9b1990dd0401385418c9c545e4be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+4=2560$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> which indeed works! <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77e4ec769f79a3c7ebf4799aa4fdc7af4a3e942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=639$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Finally, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14cd12ef8d52672dd14146e4275e3c6788e45c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=n^2-1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> so the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb05bc7fdb2efac3675f88d9a6acafbb9338402c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11-3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"135\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~xHypotenuse\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Quadratic_Residues.2C_Answer_Choices_rather_than_finding_.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Quadratic_Residues,_Answer_Choices_rather_than_finding_)\">Solution 5 (Quadratic Residues, Answer Choices rather than finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Quadratic Residues, Answer Choices rather than finding )\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every perfect square modulo 4 must end in 0 or 1 modulo 4. Reducing modulo 4 yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95d781485fc558ca78cc553b5d8a2f595a080572.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M + 1 \\pmod{4}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95d781485fc558ca78cc553b5d8a2f595a080572.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M + 1 \\pmod{4}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Both values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> yield the same result meaning that the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is unchanged through constriction. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b68691baa4bad321e5faeabacbaec95770cceeec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\equiv 3, 0 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. Analyzing the answer choices, only 3 and 8 work.\n</p><p>Now consider quadratic residue's modulo 7. Once again, they are either 0, 1, 2, 4 modulo 7. Reducing, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e7527f2b4a819f7606404aa9f56ec30096a8b82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M + 2 \\pmod{7}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d777b81ea342c1d35a3800eeac9e7041b79d11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M \\pmod{7}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is 3, we arise at a contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6acf9c4295c22d86aa9ff0726e96279b0ecb4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> can never satisfy a perfect square. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad41c3d182bfa2c0842e809cc1bf8f8fd196f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\pmod{10} = \\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"147\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>~ Extremely minor spelling correction by JAYDENK26\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 6 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Squares can only end in 0,1,4,6,5, and 9. To have x+3 (since 1213 and 3773 end in 3) end in one of those numbers and be maximized, it would be 8, because 8+3=11. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76d48d78e1726b4b56561f94556b517bfe4290d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MinglePringle348\n</p><p><br />\nNote: This solution is just a lucky fake solve; please look at the other solutions. The note below this gives a good idea of why the solution is not meaningful. M is uniquely constrained by defined distances from two perfect squares. There is no \"maximizing\" M, you simply have to solve for it algebraically.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We experiment with values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to find the reason for why <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is maximised when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d232e087b52ae9859cf821ed799cc08b83f01635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5ec4e8590af6828ae342f7e7af0f3a360d50b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> are nearly consecutive perfect squares. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is very small, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d232e087b52ae9859cf821ed799cc08b83f01635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5ec4e8590af6828ae342f7e7af0f3a360d50b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> are perfect squares that are far apart. Yet, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> grows, the relative distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d232e087b52ae9859cf821ed799cc08b83f01635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 1213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5ec4e8590af6828ae342f7e7af0f3a360d50b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + 3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> decreases, so for very nearly consecutive perfect squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is very large.\n</p><p>~LeonQS\n</p><p>(I don't know if this is trivial - when I first read the solutions, I was confused to why this was true. Maybe I didn't get enough sleep.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Apex_STEM\">Video Solution by Apex STEM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Apex STEM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-vQKjpaYe5w\">https://youtu.be/-vQKjpaYe5w</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast.21_About_3_min_solve.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast!_About_3_min_solve!)\">Video Solution (Fast! About 3 min solve!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast! About 3 min solve!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I\">https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I</a>\n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.284_min_solve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(4_min_solve)\">Video Solution (4 min solve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (4 min solve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YgJ23mepN0Q\">https://youtu.be/YgJ23mepN0Q</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ABkKz0gS1MU?si=ZQBgDMRaJmMPSSMM\">https://youtu.be/ABkKz0gS1MU?si=ZQBgDMRaJmMPSSMM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FvZVn0h3Yk4\">https://youtu.be/FvZVn0h3Yk4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CmIPAvwtWLA?si=ZCv3ypdDmCaV-aX3\">https://youtu.be/CmIPAvwtWLA?si=ZCv3ypdDmCaV-aX3</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XLoetj5obYE\">https://youtu.be/XLoetj5obYE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=2808s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=2808s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_MaffyTaffy\">Video solution by MaffyTaffy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_